"paper":"short","role":"statement","section":"2. Guerra’s interpolation and overlap estimates","start_byte":5617}]},"talagrand-parisi.proposition-5.7":{"lean":[{"end_line":189,"fidelity":"different","fidelity_note":"The paper states Ψ(t,u) < 2ψ(t) outside the two neighboring breakpoints. Lean assumes β ≠ 0 and exact SK covariance and, for each fixed scheme, level, t and u in this region, gives a positive deficit uniform in all positive sizes and disorders realizing u. The strict breakpoints in the paper exclude q₁ = 0, which Lean permits.","fidelity_source":"ai","line":174,"lines":[174,185],"module":"Targets.Section5Proposition57","name":"SpinGlass.Targets.talagrand_proposition_5_7","note":"","plain":"Strict gap past adjacent breakpoints","proof_lines":[186,189],"relation":"states"}],"short":"Strict gap beyond neighboring breakpoints","statements":[{"anchor":"sec-5","at":"b7941-8117","end_byte":8117,"heading_id":"the-quadratic-overlap-penalty","lean":[{"name":"SpinGlass.Targets.talagrand_proposition_5_7"}],"lean_source":"record","origin":"ai","paper":"short","role":"statement","section":"5. The quadratic overlap penalty","start_byte":7941}]},"talagrand-parisi.theorem-1.1":{"lean":[{"end_line":39,"fidelity":"weaker","fidelity_note":"Theorem 1.1 treats centred Gaussian Hamiltonians satisfying (1.3) for a three-times continuously differentiable, even ξ with ξ(0) = 0 and ξ″(x) > 0 for x > 0. Lean assumes β > 0 and covariance exactly Nβ²R²/2 at each size. In the off-diagonal model (1.1), the normalized covariance error β²/(2N) is removed by adding the same independent centred Gaussian of variance β²/2 to every energy, which preserves the expected log partition function.","fidelity_source":"ai","line":33,"lines":[33,36],"module":"Targets.TalagrandFinal","name":"SpinGlass.Targets.parisi_formula","note":"","plain":"The Parisi formula for SK","proof_lines":[37,39],"relation":"states"}],"short":"Theorem 1.1. The Parisi formula","statements":[{"anchor":"sec-1","at":"b1589-1738","end_byte":1738,"heading_id":"the-sk-model-and-the-parisi-formula","lean":[{"name":"SpinGlass.Targets.parisi_formula"}],"lean_source":"record","origin":"ai","paper":"short","role":"statement","section":"1. The SK model and the Parisi formula","start_byte":1589}]},"talagrand-parisi.theorem-2.1":{"lean":[{"end_line":3252,"fidelity":"weaker","fidelity_note":"In (2.10) the derivative is minus the deterministic correction and the displayed overlap term, up to an error bounded by c(N). Lean uses the exact SK covariance and states the identity through a remainder between 0 and β². The proof takes that remainder to be β²/4 times the mass-weighted replica average of (R − q)².","fidelity_source":"ai","line":3238,"lines":[3238,3243],"module":"Targets.TalagrandCore","name":"SpinGlass.Targets.guerra_identity","note":"","plain":"Guerra’s pressure derivative","proof_lines":[3244,3252],"relation":"states"}],"short":"Theorem 2.1. Guerra’s derivative formula","statements":[{"anchor":"sec-2","at":"b2664-2854","end_byte":2854,"heading_id":"guerras-interpolation-and-overlap-estimates","lean":[{"name":"SpinGlass.Targets.guerra_identity"}],"lean_source":"record","origin":"ai","paper":"short","role":"statement","section":"2. Guerra’s interpolation and overlap estimates","start_byte":2664}]},"talagrand-parisi.theorem-2.2":{"lean":[{"end_line":29,"fidelity":"weaker","fidelity_note":"For each t₀ < 1, the paper and Lean choose ε before the number of levels and the scheme. For a fixed-level minimizer within ε of the global infimum, they give pointwise convergence to ψ(t) for 0 ≤ t ≤ t₀. Lean assumes β > 0 and exact SK covariance at each size.","fidelity_source":"ai","line":21,"lines":[21,28],"module":"Targets.TalagrandFinal","name":"SpinGlass.Targets.talagrand_theorem_2_2","note":"","plain":"Convergence before time one","proof_lines":[29,29],"relation":"states"}],"short":"Convergence below time one","statements":[{"anchor":"sec-2","at":"b3317-3520","end_byte":3520,"heading_id":"guerras-interpolation-and-overlap-estimates","lean":[{"name":"SpinGlass.Targets.talagrand_theorem_2_2"}],"lean_source":"record","origin":"ai","paper":"short","role":"statement","section":"2. Guerra’s interpolation and overlap estimates","start_byte":3317}]},"talagrand-parisi.theorem-2.4":{"lean":[{"end_line":95,"fidelity":"different","fidelity_note":"The paper’s bound (2.29) includes the covariance error $2c(N)$. Lean assumes exact SK covariance and $\\beta\\ne0$ and gives the bound for sufficiently large sizes and $0<t<t_0$. The physical breakpoints must increase strictly, and the first or last may coincide with the corresponding fixed endpoint.","fidelity_source":"ai","line":76,"lines":[76,90],"module":"Targets.TalagrandTheorem24","name":"SpinGlass.Targets.talagrand_theorem_2_4","note":"","plain":"Uniform quadratic overlap penalty","proof_lines":[91,95],"relation":"states"}],"short":"Quadratic bound on constrained pressure","statements":[{"anchor":"sec-2","at":"b5401-5615","end_byte":5615,"heading_id":"guerras-interpolation-and-overlap-estimates","lean":[{"name":"SpinGlass.Targets.talagrand_theorem_2_4"}],"lean_source":"record","origin":"ai","paper":"short","role":"statement","section":"2. Guerra’s interpolation and overlap estimates","start_byte":5401}]}},"representation":"alignment_core","steps":{"talagrand-parisi.claim-guerra-upper-bound→talagrand-parisi.theorem-2.1→supports":{"route":["SpinGlass.Targets.guerra_rsb_bound","SpinGlass.Targets.guerra_identity"]},"talagrand-parisi.theorem-1.1→talagrand-parisi.claim-guerra-upper-bound→supports":{"route":["SpinGlass.Targets.parisi_formula","SpinGlass.Targets.parisi_formula_of_theorem_2_2","SpinGlass.Targets.limsup_free_entropy_le_parisiValue","SpinGlass.Targets.guerra_rsb_bound"]},"talagrand-parisi.theorem-1.1→talagrand-parisi.theorem-2.1→supports":{"route":["SpinGlass.Targets.parisi_formula","SpinGlass.Targets.parisi_formula_of_theorem_2_2","SpinGlass.Targets.guerra_identity"]},"talagrand-parisi.theorem-1.1→talagrand-parisi.theor